  "context": "## Event Intelligence\nLuxury Operations · Demand Intelligence · Event Technology Rationalization · Diamond Inside\n\nIn high-end luxury, event management and demand intelligence sit at the core of how value is created.\n\nThe mobility-orchestration account offers a comparison for demand under service commitments. Specify which groups or obligations are indivisible, which priorities are binding and who may choose trade-offs. Preserve negative demand as an uncertain signal rather than silently interpreting every non-purchase as rejection.\n\nDemand management is not only a forecasting exercise. It is the art of deciding where to place scarcity, how many pieces to produce, which markets receive which allocations, and which clients are allowed to know that certain products exist.\n\nEvent management operates on the same axis. A private event is a highly orchestrated environment where the guest list, the information revealed, the product selection and the experience itself are strategic decisions.\nTags: Agents and distributed coordination 22.73%; Authority, permissions and delegation 9.09%; Decisions and responsibility 18.18%; Business and management 31.82%; Memory, community and territory 9.09%; Representation and formal boundaries 9.09%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/event-intelligence-e1563/\nSource document: https://jubap.eu/high-end-event-intelligence-demand-orchestration/\n\n",
